title: $:/plugins/collaborative-blog/readme

! Collaborative Blog

Turns TiddlyWiki into a blog-style website for small organizations: a sidebar menu, a home page with featured and recent posts, an archive, category pages, search, five themes and special layouts for events, galleries, videos and quotes.

Editors choose ''Admin'' at the bottom of the sidebar to create and edit posts, then ''Save changes'' to publish. With the Cloudflare starter kit, saving commits the site to GitHub and Cloudflare Pages republishes it within about a minute.

!! Where things are

* ''Blog settings'': Control Panel, ''Blog'' tab (or the admin panel)
* ''Publishing'': Control Panel, ''Saving'' tab, ''Publishing'' (or the Blog tab)
* ''Setup guide'': [[$:/plugins/collaborative-blog/saver/setup-guide]]

!! Writing posts

A post is any tiddler tagged `Post`. Other tags become categories, except the reserved tags `Page`, `Featured`, `Favorite`, `Draft`, `Event`, `Gallery`, `Video` and `Quote`. The editor shows a ''Post details'' form for the author, date, excerpt and the extra fields each post type uses.

A page (About, Contact and so on) is any tiddler tagged `Page`. Add pages to the sidebar under ''Blog settings > Menu''.

''Drafts'' are hidden from lists and search, but they are still inside the published file, so do not put anything confidential in a draft.

Full documentation: https://github.com/BenSweaterVest/TiddlySite
